    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  The <span class='learn-keyword'>public service</span> (civil service) is the body of officials who implement government policy and deliver services to citizens. Understanding its role, the duties of public servants, and the responsibilities of citizens toward the public service is central to good citizenship.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Meaning of Public Service</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>The public service (often used interchangeably with civil service) refers to permanent, professional government employees — such as those in ministries, departments and agencies — who carry out the day-to-day work of government under the direction of elected or appointed political leaders. Unlike political office holders, career civil servants are expected to remain politically neutral.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Roles of the Civil Service</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Policy implementation</td><td>Carries out government policies and programmes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Advisory role</td><td>Advises ministers and political office holders on technical matters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Service delivery</td><td>Provides public services (health, education, revenue collection, etc.)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Record keeping</td><td>Maintains government records and continuity across administrations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Regulation</td><td>Enforces laws and regulations affecting citizens and businesses</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Duties of Public Servants and Citizens</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Public servants owe duties of loyalty, integrity, political neutrality, confidentiality, and diligence. Citizens, in turn, have a duty to respect lawful public service processes, pay taxes that fund public service, report corruption, and engage constructively with public institutions.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Challenges of the Public Service</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Common challenges include corruption, bureaucratic bottlenecks (red tape), inadequate funding, poor remuneration leading to low morale, political interference, and skills gaps. Addressing these challenges requires reforms such as merit-based recruitment, digitalization (e-governance), and anti-corruption measures.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish civil servants (career, permanent, politically neutral) from political office holders (elected/appointed, serve for a term, can be partisan). This distinction is commonly tested.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The public service implements government policy, delivers services, and advises political leadership. It faces challenges like corruption and red tape, and citizens have duties to support and hold it accountable.\n</div>\n  ",
