    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  Nigeria's <span class='learn-keyword'>colonial heritage</span> refers to the lasting legacies — both positive and negative — left behind by British colonial rule (roughly 1861 to 1960). Evaluating this heritage helps citizens understand present-day institutions, challenges, and opportunities shaped by that history.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Background</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>British colonization of Nigeria progressed from the annexation of Lagos in 1861 through the amalgamation of the Northern and Southern Protectorates in 1914 by Lord Lugard, to independence in 1960. Colonial rule fundamentally reshaped Nigeria's political boundaries, economy, and social structures.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Positive Impacts of Colonial Rule</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Positive Impact</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Infrastructure</td><td>Introduction of railways, roads, ports, and telecommunications</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Education</td><td>Introduction of Western formal education and mission schools</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Administration</td><td>Introduction of modern civil service and unified territorial administration</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Health</td><td>Introduction of Western medicine and hospitals</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Unification</td><td>Amalgamation of diverse regions into one country, Nigeria (1914)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Negative Impacts of Colonial Rule</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Negative legacies include the arbitrary amalgamation of diverse ethnic groups without regard to cultural compatibility, exploitation of natural resources and labour for the benefit of the colonial power, disruption of indigenous political and economic systems, the introduction of divisive indirect rule that deepened regional and ethnic divisions, and cultural erosion as indigenous customs and languages were sometimes suppressed.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Lessons from Colonial Heritage</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Studying colonial heritage teaches Nigerians the importance of national unity despite diversity, the need to build strong indigenous institutions, the value of resource control and self-reliance, and the importance of learning from history to avoid repeating patterns of exploitation and division.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to list BOTH positive and negative impacts of colonialism — exam questions often ask for a balanced evaluation, not just criticism or praise alone.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Colonial heritage left Nigeria with infrastructure, education, and administrative systems (positives), but also arbitrary unification, exploitation, and ethnic division (negatives) — lessons that inform national development today.\n</div>\n  ",
