    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  The <span class='learn-keyword'>preservation of historical records</span> — through archives, museums, and libraries — ensures that Nigeria's past is documented, protected, and accessible for research, education, and national identity, both now and for future generations.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Meaning and Importance</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Historical records include documents, photographs, artefacts, and oral histories that capture past events, decisions, and cultures. Preserving them safeguards evidence of national history, supports legal and administrative continuity, informs policy-making, and enables citizens to learn from the past.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Institutions for Preservation</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Institution</th><th>Function</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>National Archives of Nigeria</td><td>Preserves government records, colonial documents, and official papers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>National Library of Nigeria</td><td>Collects and preserves published works, serves as legal deposit library</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Museums (NCMM-managed)</td><td>Preserve physical artefacts and cultural objects</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Universities and Research Institutes</td><td>House specialized archives and conduct historical research</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Digital Archives</td><td>Increasingly used to digitize and preserve records against physical decay</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Methods of Preservation</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Methods include proper physical storage (climate-controlled archives), digitization/scanning of documents, microfilming, oral history recording, restoration of damaged artefacts, and legal deposit laws requiring publishers to submit copies of works to national repositories.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Challenges</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Challenges include inadequate funding, poor storage facilities leading to deterioration, loss of records to fire, flood, insects, or theft, low public awareness of archival value, and slow adoption of digital preservation technology.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish the roles of the National Archives (official government records) from the National Library (published works/legal deposit) and museums (physical artefacts) — exams often test which institution handles which type of record.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Preserving historical records through archives, libraries, and museums safeguards Nigeria's documented past, supporting research, education, and national identity, despite challenges like poor funding and deterioration.\n</div>\n  ",
