    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  <span class='learn-keyword'>Governance</span> refers to the process by which a country's affairs are managed and decisions are made and implemented. Understanding its meaning, principles, and systems helps citizens appreciate their role in ensuring accountable and effective government.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Meaning of Governance</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Governance is the exercise of political, economic, and administrative authority to manage a nation's affairs. It involves the processes and institutions through which decisions are made, implemented, and citizens' interests are represented, extending beyond just government to include the participation of civil society and the private sector.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Principles of Good Governance</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Accountability</td><td>Government officials answer for their decisions and actions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Transparency</td><td>Open, accessible decision-making processes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Rule of Law</td><td>Laws apply equally to all, including leaders</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Participation</td><td>Citizens have a voice in decisions that affect them</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Responsiveness</td><td>Government institutions serve the needs of citizens promptly</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Equity/Inclusiveness</td><td>Fair treatment of all groups regardless of background</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Systems of Governance</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Governance systems vary globally: <strong>democracy</strong> (rule by the people through elected representatives), <strong>monarchy</strong> (rule by a hereditary king/queen), <strong>military rule</strong> (governance by armed forces, often after a coup), <strong>autocracy/dictatorship</strong> (rule by one person with unchecked power), and <strong>theocracy</strong> (rule guided primarily by religious authority). Nigeria currently practices a democratic, federal, presidential system of governance.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Governance is broader than 'government' — governance includes processes and the roles of civil society, private sector, and citizens, not just formal state institutions.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Governance is the process of managing a nation's affairs guided by principles like accountability, transparency, and participation. Nigeria practices democratic governance, one of several possible systems worldwide.\n</div>\n  ",
