    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  National <span class='learn-keyword'>security</span> is the protection of a nation, its citizens, and institutions from threats. Security is not only the responsibility of security agencies like the police and army — citizens themselves have important roles to play in maintaining safety and order.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Roles of Key Security Agencies</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Agency</th><th>Primary Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Nigeria Police Force</td><td>Internal law enforcement, crime prevention, maintaining public order</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Nigerian Army/Armed Forces</td><td>Defense against external aggression; internal security support (e.g., counter-insurgency)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Civil Defence (NSCDC)</td><td>Protection of critical infrastructure, civil protection, disaster response support</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>State Security Service (SSS/DSS)</td><td>Domestic intelligence gathering and internal security threats</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Vigilante/Community Watch groups</td><td>Local, citizen-led community security support</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Citizens' Roles in Security</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Citizens contribute to security by reporting suspicious activities, cooperating with lawful security operations, participating in community policing or neighbourhood watch initiatives, avoiding actions that fuel insecurity (such as hate speech or violence), and supporting peaceful conflict resolution.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Contemporary Security Challenges in Nigeria</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Nigeria faces security challenges including terrorism/insurgency (e.g., in the North-East), banditry and kidnapping, farmer-herder conflicts, cultism, cybercrime, and separatist agitations. Addressing these requires coordinated efforts between security agencies, government, and citizens.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Balancing Security and Rights</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>While security is essential, it must be pursued in ways that respect citizens' human rights and the rule of law. Excessive or abusive use of force by security agencies can itself become a source of insecurity and public distrust.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to distinguish the roles of the Police (internal law enforcement) from the Armed Forces (external defense, though increasingly used internally) — a frequently tested distinction.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Security involves the police, army, and civil defence, but also requires active citizen participation through vigilance, cooperation, and peaceful conduct, all while respecting human rights.\n</div>\n  ",
