    "term": "Third Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  <span class='learn-keyword'>Elections</span> are the process by which citizens choose their leaders and representatives through voting. Elections are the cornerstone of democracy, and understanding voter eligibility, the voting process, and civic duties around elections is central to responsible citizenship.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Meaning and Importance of Elections</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Elections allow citizens to exercise their political power by choosing representatives to govern on their behalf. Regular, free, and fair elections legitimize government authority, enable peaceful transfer of power, and hold leaders accountable to the electorate.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Voter Eligibility and Registration</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Under Nigerian law, a citizen is eligible to vote if they are at least 18 years old, are a Nigerian citizen, and are registered with INEC (obtaining a Permanent Voter Card, PVC). Voter registration is a prerequisite that establishes a citizen's legal right to cast a ballot.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. The Voting Process</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Voter registration</td><td>Citizens register and obtain a Permanent Voter Card (PVC)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Accreditation</td><td>Voters are verified at polling units on election day (e.g., using the Bimodal Voter Accreditation System, BVAS)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Voting</td><td>Citizens cast their ballot in secret at their designated polling unit</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Collation</td><td>Votes are counted and results collated at ward, LGA, state and national levels</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Declaration</td><td>INEC officially announces the results</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Civic Duties Around Elections</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Citizens have duties to register and obtain their PVC, vote responsibly based on informed judgment, avoid vote-selling or buying, respect the outcome of credible elections, and, where dissatisfied, pursue lawful means (like the courts) rather than violence to challenge results.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the minimum voting age (18) and the acronym PVC (Permanent Voter Card) and BVAS (Bimodal Voter Accreditation System) — these are frequently tested factual points.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Elections let citizens choose leaders through a structured process of registration, accreditation, voting, and collation. Responsible citizenship includes registering, voting wisely, and respecting lawful outcomes.\n</div>\n  ",
