    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  The <span class='learn-keyword'>mass media</span> — newspapers, radio, television, and increasingly social media — plays a powerful role in shaping public opinion, holding government accountable, and informing citizens' participation in democracy.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Roles of the Media in a Democracy</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Information dissemination</td><td>Keeping citizens informed about government, events, and issues</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Watchdog / accountability</td><td>Investigating and exposing corruption, abuse of power, and wrongdoing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Public opinion formation</td><td>Shaping how citizens perceive issues, leaders, and policies</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Civic education</td><td>Educating citizens about their rights, duties, and how government works</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Platform for expression</td><td>Providing space for citizens and groups to voice opinions and concerns</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. The Media as the 'Fourth Estate'</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>The media is often called the 'Fourth Estate' because, alongside the Executive, Legislature, and Judiciary, it serves as an informal but powerful check on government power by informing the public and exposing misconduct — essential for a healthy democracy.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Responsible Media Use by Citizens</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Citizens are encouraged to consume news critically, verify information from multiple credible sources, avoid spreading unverified claims or hate speech, and use social media responsibly, recognizing both its power to inform and its potential to spread misinformation quickly.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Challenges Facing the Media</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Challenges include censorship and government pressure on journalists, the spread of 'fake news' and disinformation especially on social media, commercial pressures compromising editorial independence, and safety risks for journalists reporting on sensitive or dangerous topics.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the term 'Fourth Estate' as a description of the media's role in checking government power alongside the three formal arms — this term is a common exam feature.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The media informs, educates, and holds government accountable as the 'Fourth Estate'. Citizens must use media responsibly, verifying information and avoiding the spread of misinformation.\n</div>\n  ",
