    "topic": "Civic Challenges",
    "topicCode": "SS2-CHS-22",
    "module": "Civic Responsibility",
    "term": "Third Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  Nigeria faces several ongoing <span class='learn-keyword'>civic challenges</span> that hinder national progress and citizens' quality of life, including corruption, unemployment, and ethnic/religious tensions. Understanding these challenges equips citizens to be part of the solution.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Corruption</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Corruption involves the abuse of entrusted power for private gain, including bribery, embezzlement, and nepotism. It diverts public resources meant for development, weakens institutions, and undermines citizens' trust in government. Agencies like the EFCC and ICPC exist to combat corrupt practices.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Unemployment</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Unemployment, especially among Nigeria's large youth population, contributes to poverty, social unrest, and can push some individuals toward crime or extremism. Causes include a mismatch between education/skills and job market needs, slow economic growth, and inadequate investment in job-creating sectors.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Ethnic and Religious Tensions</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Nigeria's diversity of over 250 ethnic groups and multiple religions is a strength, but can also be a source of tension when politicized or when resources/appointments are perceived as unfairly distributed along ethnic or religious lines, sometimes fueling conflict or mistrust.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Challenge</th><th>Key Impact</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Corruption</td><td>Diverts resources, weakens institutions, erodes public trust</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Unemployment</td><td>Increases poverty, social unrest, vulnerability to crime</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ethnic/religious tension</td><td>Can fuel conflict, mistrust, and hinder national unity</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Citizens' Roles in Addressing These Challenges</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Citizens can combat corruption by refusing to participate in or report it; address unemployment by pursuing skills development and supporting local entrepreneurship; and ease ethnic/religious tension by promoting tolerance, dialogue, and rejecting divisive rhetoric in their communities and online spaces.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Learn the names of Nigeria's key anti-corruption agencies (EFCC, ICPC) and be ready to link each civic challenge to at least one practical citizen-level solution.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Nigeria faces civic challenges like corruption, unemployment, and ethnic/religious tension, each requiring both institutional reform and active, responsible citizen engagement to address effectively.\n</div>\n  ",
