    "contentHTML": "\n<div class='learn-intro'>\n  <span class='learn-keyword'>National development</span> refers to the overall improvement in a country's economic, social, political, and human conditions over time. It requires coordinated effort from government, institutions, and individual citizens.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>1. Meaning and Dimensions of National Development</h3>\n<div class='learn-table-wrap'>\n  <table class='learn-table'>\n    <thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Economic development</td><td>Growth in income, industry, infrastructure, and job creation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Social development</td><td>Improvements in health, education, and general welfare</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Political development</td><td>Strengthening democratic institutions, rule of law, and good governance</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Human development</td><td>Enhancing citizens' skills, knowledge, and quality of life</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>2. Indicators of National Development</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Indicators used to measure development include Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and per capita income, literacy and school enrollment rates, life expectancy and access to healthcare, employment rates, and broader measures like the Human Development Index (HDI), which combines income, education, and health.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>3. Factors that Promote National Development</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Key drivers include good governance and strong institutions, investment in education and human capital, infrastructure development (power, roads, technology), a stable and diversified economy, and peace and security that enable productive economic activity.</p>\n\n<h3 class='learn-subheading'>4. Citizens' Role in National Development</h3>\n<p class='learn-p'>Citizens contribute to development through hard work and productivity, paying taxes honestly, obeying laws, participating in civic and political life, supporting local enterprise, and using their skills and talents constructively for the benefit of their communities and the nation.</p>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Learn the four dimensions of development (economic, social, political, human) and be ready to classify a given example (e.g., 'building more hospitals') under the correct dimension.\n</div>\n\n<div class='learn-tip-box'>\n  <span class='learn-tip-icon'>🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> National development spans economic, social, political, and human dimensions, measured by indicators like GDP and HDI, and driven by good governance, education, infrastructure, and active citizen participation.\n</div>\n  ",
